<title>POLAND: Polish broad money rises 0.5 pct in Feb 1-20 - NBP.</title>
<headline>Polish broad money rises 0.5 pct in Feb 1-20 - NBP.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's broad money rose by 679.1 million zlotys ($220.5 million), or 0.5 percent, in February 1-20 to 136.72 billion after a 0.1-percent rise in January, preliminary central bank figures showed.  </p>
<p> BROAD POLISH MONEY			FEB 1-20   JAN 97   FEB 96</p>
<p>  month/month change (pct)		0.5	  0.1	 2.5</p>
<p>  Money in bln zlotys		   136.72     136.04    108.12</p>
<p>  Foreign currency (in bln PLN)	24.57	24.26     21.37</p>
<p>  National currency		     112.15     111.79     86.75</p>
<p>  Cash in circulation		    22.31	22.77     20.18</p>
<p>  Lending to non-financial sector    84.42	83.33     58.28</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
